From 6aaced82eff8b3d6d4efd4e12bb18ea132c61602 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:21:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bcmgenetd: Ethernet of the Raspberry Pi 4 and 400 (BCM2711
 GENET v5)

A network scheme driver for the GENET v5 controller with its BCM54213PE
PHY: one receive and one transmit ring (the default queue 16), receive
and transmit interrupts, MDIO for the link, a link check every second.
The MAC address comes from the devicetree, else from the controller (left
there by U-Boot), else from the serial number. The PHY keeps the setup
the firmware or U-Boot gave it.

The register layout follows FreeBSD if_genet.c (BSD-2-Clause); no GPL
code was used. Register, ring, MDIO and devicetree logic is a library
with host unit tests (cargo test --lib).

redox-rpi #306.
